{"fingerprint":"20830371f41a197612b36eed2cb3a0cc777436cae33ac85cf9b43f08c63fc4b8","path":"src/auth/clipboard.rs","rule_id":"cli-contract","content":"Linux clipboard helper discovery only tries to execute each helper with `--version` (and then the same binary with `-v`), so a helper that exists but does not support those flags or exits non-zero will be treated as unavailable even though the subsequent stdin-based invocation would work. That makes clipboard copy fail unnecessarily in otherwise valid CLI environments. Prefer PATH lookup that does not execute the helper with tool-specific flags, or just attempt `try_command_with_stdin` and rely on spawn failure for missing commands.","suggestion_code":"fn command_exists(cmd: &str) -> bool {
    std::env::var_os("PATH")
        .and_then(|paths| {
            std::env::split_paths(&paths)
                .map(|path| path.join(cmd))
                .find(|path| path.is_file())
        })
        .is_some()
}","existing_code":"fn command_exists(cmd: &str) -> bool {
